  "question": {
    "text": "Two circles with centers at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> touch each other externally at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>.&nbsp;Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BD</mi></math> is the tangent at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is a common tangent. If&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> has length <math><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;units and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> has length <math><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;units, then&nbsp;the length (in units) of&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/e84e5d5e-70c6-4bf8-8f2e-50bcdc0c1119.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.96667in;height:1.12708in\" />",
    "image": null
  },
